\tag{fdip}
\title{The bulk integer and the index in a field}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{A scalar link field on an oriented torus has an integer [plaquette flux](fdip-015V). The regular Hermitian operator formed by multiplying the Wilson kernel by its grading has an index read from the dimensions of its positive and negative parts (\ref{fdip-0155}). How does the mass enter the relation between these integers?}

\p{The coordinate order fixes the orientation. The forward shift uses the inverse link as in the [covariant centered difference](fdip-009O). The two-dimensional comparison concerns the phases on one scalar line, including when several spin or fiber copies carry that same phase.}

